{
    "type": "Collection",
    "id": "PACE_OCI_L1B_CLOSE_3",
    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "Level 1B (L1B) data are Level 1A (L1A) data that have been processed to instrument units (not all instruments have L1B source data).\nThe Closed-Loop Ocean Simulation for Evaluation of ocean color retrieval algorithms (CLOSE) Level-1B collection provides simulated PACE OCI top-of-atmosphere observations generated by PyTOAST from the CLOSE model inputs. The files contain top-of-atmosphere reflectances for the blue, red, and shortwave-infrared bands, along with geolocation, viewing geometry, navigation, scan timing, spectral-response, calibration, and quality information. These simulated observations support atmospheric-correction testing and controlled evaluation of ocean-color retrieval algorithms.\n\n Principal variables and supporting data in this collection include:\n - rhot_blue \u2014 Top-of-atmosphere reflectance for OCI blue bands\n - rhot_red \u2014 Top-of-atmosphere reflectance for OCI red bands\n - rhot_SWIR \u2014 Top-of-atmosphere reflectance for OCI shortwave-infrared bands\n - qual_blue, qual_red, and qual_SWIR \u2014 Spectral-band quality flags\n - latitude and longitude \u2014 Pixel geolocation\n - sensor_azimuth and sensor_zenith \u2014 Sensor-viewing geometry\n - solar_azimuth and solar_zenith \u2014 Solar geometry\n - height \u2014 Terrain height at pixel locations\n - watermask and quality_flag \u2014 Surface classification and geolocation quality information\n - CCD_scan_angles and SWIR_scan_angles \u2014 Instrument scan angles\n - att_ang and att_quat \u2014 Spacecraft attitude information\n - orb_pos and orb_vel \u2014 Orbit position and velocity\n - sun_ref \u2014 Solar reference vectors\n - tilt_angle \u2014 OCI tilt angle\n - time, HAM_side, and scan_quality_flags \u2014 Scan-line timing and quality information\n - blue_wavelength, red_wavelength, and SWIR_wavelength \u2014 Band-center wavelengths\n - blue_solar_irradiance, red_solar_irradiance, and SWIR_solar_irradiance \u2014 Mean extraterrestrial solar irradiance\n - Blue, red, and SWIR bandpass and polarization-coefficient information",
